## Why This Problem Is Asked

This question tests dynamic programming on partitioning with a non-linear cost function (block maximum). It extends beyond standard max-sum variants and evaluates careful indexing, prefix handling, and solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- **Contiguous partition DP**: State dp[i][t] represents the minimum cost for the prefix of length i using exactly t blocks
- **Transition**: Computes the running maximum for the last block while finding the optimal split point
- **Reconstruction**: Backtracking through the DP table to determine block endpoints

## Code Example

```javascript
function minSumOfBlockMax(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const split = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = Math.max(...A.slice(0, i));
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      let maxVal = 0;
      for (let j = i - 1; j >= t - 1; j--) {
        maxVal = Math.max(maxVal, A[j]);
        const cost = dp[j][t - 1] + maxVal;
        if (cost < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = cost;
          split[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = split[i][t];
    blocks.unshift({ start: j + 1, end: i });
    i = j;
    t--;
  }

  return { minSum: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays, a common beginner challenge with practical reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- dp[i][t]: best sum using first i elements with exactly t subarrays
- end[i][t]: best subarray sum ending at i-1 for t subarrays
- Transitions combine extending a subarray or starting a new one
- Reconstruction via backtracking boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      end[i][t] = Math.max(end[i-1][t] + A[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], end[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n][k]};
}
```

